## Run the existing pipeline

Python 3.10+ and either installed Python `jsonschema` or PowerShell 7 Draft2020-12 `Test-Json` are required. The original Windows environment used PowerShell; packages were not installed. If neither validator is available, install the official Python jsonschema package in a project virtual environment, or use an available PowerShell 7. Do not replace validation with a partial checker.

From the extracted project root:

```powershell
python -B research_pipeline.py --store work/task-04-runs validate --run-id pilot-first-pass-001
python -B research_pipeline.py --store work/task-04-runs metrics --run-id pilot-first-pass-001 --target pilot-first-pass-001
python -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_research_pipeline.py -v
```

The 23 regression tests use synthetic data only. Passing them does not measure app accuracy. Saved-evidence validation/replay needs no API key or network. Independent current-doc verification needs the agent's web/browser access, not an embedded Gemini API integration.

The agent selected and read sources and authored the structured extraction builder; the pipeline automated HTTP content capture, snapshots, hashes, packets, intake validation, immutable runs and metrics. It is not a fully automatic source-discovery/model service. No Composio or Gemini SDK integration is currently embedded.

